// Author: Calvin Quint
// GitHub: https://github.com/calvin-quint/docs/blob/main/01-detection-engineering/kql/identity-governance/pva_service_principal_owner_add.kql
// Power Virtual Agents Adding Service Principal Owner
// MITRE ATT&CK: Persistence / Privilege Escalation — Account Manipulation:
//               Additional Cloud Roles (T1098.003)
// Detects: A service principal ownership change initiated by Power Virtual
//          Agents specifically — an unusual actor for this operation. Owning
//          a service principal grants control over its credentials and
//          permissions, so a Power Platform bot/flow granting itself or
//          another principal ownership is a plausible privilege-escalation
//          path via low-code automation that's easy to overlook.
// Entity mapping: Account → UPN → userPrincipalName
AuditLogs
| where OperationName contains "Add owner to service principal"
| where tostring(InitiatedBy) contains "Power Virtual Agents"
| mv-expand TargetResources
| extend userPrincipalName = tostring(TargetResources.userPrincipalName)
